id: gatt_common
package: bluetooth_le_siwx91x
description: >
  GATT Common - Shared code and configuration for GATT Server and Client
label: GATT Common
category: Device|Si91x|Wireless|BLE|GATT
quality: production
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
component_root_path: ./components/device/silabs/si91x/wireless/gatt
provides:
  - name: gatt_common
define:
  - name: SL_SI91X_BLE_GATT_COMMON_COMPONENT
source:
  - path: common/src/gatt_common_event_hdlrs.c
  - path: common/src/gatt_common_init.c

include:
  - path: common/inc
    file_list:
      - path: gatt_common.h

config_file:
  - path: common/inc/gatt_common_config.h
    directory: ble_config
    file_id: gatt_common_config

requires:
  - name: ble_unified_framework
  - name: gap

template_contribution:
  - name: ble_unified_config_includes
    value: "gatt_common_config.h"
  - name: ble_unified_init_hooks
    value:
      ble_unified_init_func: ble_gatt_common_init
      ble_unified_init_label: "GATT Common"
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_GATT_ASYNC_ENABLE
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_guard: RSI_BLE_GATT_ASYNC_ENABLE
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_ext_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_MTU_EXCHANGE_FROM_HOST
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_guard: RSI_BLE_MTU_EXCHANGE_FROM_HOST
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_ext_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_GATT_INIT
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_guard: BLE_SIMPLE_GATT
  - name: wrapper_implementations
    value:
      name: sl_btc_ble_gatt_common_register_callbacks_wrapper
      registration_api: rsi_ble_gatt_common_register_callbacks
      callbacks:
        - event_gatt_write
  - name: ble_events
    value:
      event_gatt_write:
        callback_params:
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
          - name: rsi_ble_event_write
            type: rsi_ble_event_write_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_write
  - name: agents_slab
    value:
      id: gatt_common
      context: |
        ## GATT Common Component (Si91x Wireless BLE Unified)
        Shared GATT plumbing required by both `gatt_server` and `gatt_client`. Selected automatically when either Server or Client is selected. Defines `SL_SI91X_BLE_GATT_COMMON_COMPONENT`.
        ### Init hook
        - Function: `ble_gatt_common_init` (registered via `ble_unified_init_hooks`).
        - Registers the cross-cutting GATT-common callback wrapper `sl_btc_ble_gatt_common_register_callbacks_wrapper()` (currently `event_gatt_write` — fired on incoming write/write-without-response from a peer regardless of role).
        ### Configuration (`gatt_common_config.h` — copied to `config/ble_config/`)
        Key macros (each gated by a `*_guard` so the bitmap entry is contributed only when defined):
        - `RSI_BLE_GATT_ASYNC_ENABLE` → contributes `SL_SI91X_BLE_GATT_ASYNC_ENABLE` (async GATT command/response model — required for the modern API).
        - `RSI_BLE_MTU_EXCHANGE_FROM_HOST` → contributes `SL_SI91X_BLE_MTU_EXCHANGE_FROM_HOST` (host issues MTU exchange instead of letting the controller initiate).
        - `BLE_SIMPLE_GATT` → contributes `SL_SI91X_BLE_GATT_INIT` (legacy simple-GATT init path).
        ### Common Mistakes to Avoid
        - Selecting `gatt_server` or `gatt_client` without `gatt_common` — SLC will surface this as an unmet `requires:`, but if you wire components manually you'll get linker errors on `ble_gatt_common_init` and missing `event_gatt_write` registration.
        - Toggling `RSI_BLE_GATT_ASYNC_ENABLE` off — the BLE Unified GATT Server/Client implementations rely on the async response/event model; turning it off effectively breaks them.
        - Disabling `RSI_BLE_MTU_EXCHANGE_FROM_HOST` if your throughput-sensitive service expects a specific MTU — without host-side exchange the controller may negotiate a smaller MTU than desired.
    priority: -5305
